    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0458" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/913.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department’s instructions of March 31 were immediately complied with and the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs to-day replied to <pb facs="0459" n="343"
                        xml:id="pg343"/> my memorandum. The reply is not entirely satisfactory
                    inasmuch as the Minister for Foreign Affairs attempts to again open up the
                    entire Syrian question. Through the Chief of Bureau of Foreign Affairs, however,
                    I was informed to-day that the Haitian Consul General at New York City would be
                    instructed to vise passports in accordance with former agreements between this
                    Legation and the Haitian Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>Continued efforts will be made from day to day to satisfactorily adjust this
                    matter though it is most difficult to obtain action by the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs he being in a peculiar political situation and avoiding all possible
                    action upon foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>The entire Diplomatic Corps report inability to make any progress with pending
                    questions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
